      "message": "guess its okay but the aligned width is really a stride and/or pixel count that takes into account subsampling.  if we put it in its own variable it could be ptrdiff_t and avoid casting.  we use it in multiply by width to figure out stride so i think ptrdiff_t is the right type.  checked with a compiler/math guy and he agrees",
